          "Solution: Given, radius of the circle = 7 cm and angle of sector = 90° mrQ@ 22 7x90° Length of th f th L=— =—x—— ength of the arc of the sector 180° 7 180° or 7=11em 1 Area of the sector =5% Lix 1 77 =—x11x7=— =38.5 cn' 7 5 cm Example 4. Given figure is an equilateral triangle, whose length of one side is 20 cm. Form each of the vertex of the triangle three arcs are drawn with a radius 10 cm. Find out the area of the shaded portion.(Take m=3.14and 3 =1.73) A Solution; Given, length of the side of equilateral triangle = 20 cm.",
          "We know that, measured degree of each of the angle of an equilateral triangle = 60° There for, area of three sectors will be equal.",
