          "Solution: Given, radius of the circle r = 14 cm.",
          "Example 8. A chord in a circle radius 12 cm substeds an angle of 120° at the centre. Find the area of corresponding segment of the circle. (Take m= 3.14 and 3 =1.73) Solution: Here. r= 12 cm and 9= 120° Area of the corresponding segment = area of the minor segment = area of sector OAB — area of A OAB.... (i) Area sector OAB =—2—x tr? = 29x 3.141212 om?",
          "Exercise 15.2 1. Radius of a circle is 7 cm and the angle subtended at the centre by an arc is 60°. Find the length of the are.",
          "2. Radius of a circle is 10.5 cm and angle of the sector is 45°. Find the area of the minor sector of the 22 circle.| 7 = > 3. The length of an arc is 12 cm and radius of a circle is 7 cm respectively.",
